-- A proof-local def may carry notation declared in the proof file, written
-- exactly as in an .mm0 file. The token is proof-side sugar: later proof
-- math parses it, the .mm0 file never sees it, and the MMB carries no
-- notation at all.
def limp (a b: wff): wff = $ a -> b $
infixr limp: $=>$ prec 25;

lemma limp_k (a b: wff): $ a => b => a $
----
l1: $ a => b => a $ by ax_k []

pass_local_notation
-------------------
p: $ a => top => a $ by limp_k []
